## Step 2: Identify Pareto Front (maximize both E and PF)

Excluding clearly unreliable measurements (CV=1.02 for 17p5-15deg-120s) and noting single-specimen SD=0 cases as lower reliability.

Key candidates with good quality and both objectives:

**High E, moderate-high PF:**
- 17p5-0add-15deg-60s-N2 run1: E=519.51, PF=0.36 ✓ (good quality, 3 runs)
- 17p5-0add-15deg-60s-N2 run2: E=695.94, PF=0.26 (high E but low PF, high SD)
- 17-0add-10deg-60s-N2: E=381.81, PF=0.36 ✓ (good quality)
- 17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2 run4: E=501.80, PF=0.35 ✓ (good quality)
- 19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2 run1: E=350.75, PF=0.43 (high PF but low E, single specimen)
- 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2 run1: E=476.82, PF=0.39 (top gap defect)
- 17-0add-10deg-60s-N2: E=381.81, PF=0.36

**Pareto-non-dominated candidates (good quality, no severe defects):**

Sorting by PF descending among good-quality experiments:
- PF=0.39: E=476.82 (18-0add-15deg-600s — top gap defect, run2 has E=339.82, PF=0.32 — inconsistent)
- PF=0.36: E=519.51 (17p5-15deg-60s run1), E=381.81 (17-10deg-60s)
- PF=0.35: E=501.80 (17p5-20deg-90s run4), E=683.29 (17p5-20deg-90s run1 — single specimen SD=0)
- PF=0.33: E=516.22 (19-10deg-240s run1), E=592.77 (18p5-5deg-105s — gap defect)
- PF=0.32: E=339.82 (18-15deg-600s run2), E=419.28 (17p5-25deg-375s run2)
- PF=0.31: E=547.22 (17-5deg-30s run2), E=442.33 (17p5-10deg-90s)
- PF=0.30: E=596.31 (18-5deg-180s — wrinkles), E=449.22 (18-15deg-60s)
- PF=0.29: E=522.59 (17-10deg-90s run2), E=412.05 (17p5-10deg-60s)
- PF=0.28: E=708.94 (17p5-10deg-15s run1 — high SD), E=501.73 (17p5-5deg-60s — gap)

**Pareto front analysis** (no defect filter, good quality):

A point (E₁, PF₁) dominates (E₂, PF₂) if E₁≥E₂ AND PF₁≥PF₂ with at least one strict.

Checking non-dominated set:
- (519.51, 0.36) — run1 of 17p5-15deg-60s: dominated by anything with E≥519 AND PF≥0.36? No such point exists with good quality → **non-dominated**
- (501.80, 0.35) — run4 of 17p5-20deg-90s: dominated by (519.51, 0.36)? Yes (519>501 AND 0.36>0.35) → dominated
- (381.81, 0.36) — 17-10deg-60s: dominated by (519.51, 0.36)? Yes (519>381, same PF) → dominated
- (640.23, 0.29) — 17-15deg-90s run2: dominated by (519.51, 0.36)? No (640>519 but 0.29<0.36) → **non-dominated**
- (591.97, 0.27) — 17-15deg-90s run1: dominated by (640.23, 0.29)? Yes → dominated
- (547.22, 0.31) — 17-5deg-30s run2: dominated by (519.51, 0.36)? No (547>519 but 0.31<0.36); dominated by (640.23, 0.29)? No (0.31>0.29) → **non-dominated**
- (522.59, 0.29) — 17-10deg-90s run2: dominated by (547.22, 0.31)? Yes → dominated
- (596.34, 0.27) — 17-10deg-75s: dominated by (640.23, 0.29)? Yes → dominated

**Pareto front (good quality, no severe defects):**
1. (519.51, 0.36) — 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1 [3 runs: 519, 695, 406 — high variability across runs]
2. (547.22, 0.31) — 17-5deg-30s-N2 run2 [1 independent run]
3. (640.23, 0.29) — 17-15deg-90s-N2 run2 [2 runs: 591, 640]

