- PF=0.36, E=519.51 (run1, 17p5/15deg/60s): Not dominated — highest PF among reliable candidates with decent E
- PF=0.36, E=381.81 (17-0add-10deg-60s): Dominated by run1 (same PF, lower E)
- PF=0.35, E=501.80 (17p5/20deg/run4): Dominated by run1 (lower PF, lower E)
- PF=0.29, E=640.23 (17-0add-15deg-90s-run2): Not dominated — highest reliable E with PF=0.29
- PF=0.27, E=596.34 (17-0add-10deg-75s): Dominated by 640.23/0.29
- PF=0.27, E=591.97 (17-0add-15deg-90s): Dominated by 640.23/0.29

**Approximate Pareto front (reliable candidates):**
1. **17p5-0add-15deg-60s (run1)**: E=519.51, PF=0.36 — highest PF
2. **17-0add-15deg-90s-run2**: E=640.23, PF=0.29 — highest reliable E

The gap between these two is the key trade-off region. The ideal next experiment would try to find a point with E > 519 AND PF > 0.29 — a true Pareto improvement.

