**17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2 (run4)**: E=501.80, PF=0.35 with CV=0.15, good quality membrane. This is potentially Pareto-superior to 17-0add-15deg-90s-run2 (E=640, PF=0.29) in the PF dimension, and superior to 17p5-0add-15deg-60s runs in the E dimension. Only one reliable multi-specimen measurement exists. This warrants validation.

**17p5-0add-15deg-60s**: Highly variable across 4 runs — not a stable candidate.

**17-0add-10deg-60s-N2**: E=381.81, PF=0.36 — only one run, needs validation for the high-PF claim.

## Step 5: Decision

The strongest unvalidated Pareto candidate with a single reliable multi-specimen measurement is **17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2 (run4 conditions)**: polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=20, mixing_temp=50, pullcast_speed=7, nitrogen=True, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=90, nips_bath_wait_time=1250. This showed E=501.80 bar and PF=0.35 — if reproducible, this would be Pareto-non-dominated (higher PF than the confirmed E~616/PF~0.28 point, with competitive E). The original run1 was n=1 fit and unreliable; run4 is the first reliable measurement. A validation repeat is warranted before treating this as a confirmed Pareto improvement.

